    "depth": 0,
    "payload": {
      "content": "The best checkpoint achieved precision 0.998, recall 1.000, mAP50\n0.994, and mAP50–95 0.961 on the validation set (Table 2). During infer-\nence, we applied non-maximum suppression (IoU = 0.50) and retained \nonly the top-1 detection per image (max_det= 1), thereby removing \nany overlapping proposals. A symmetric 3% margin was added before \ncropping to avoid truncating the blade tip or guard, and the crop \nwas resized to 512 × 512. Detections with low confidence, abnormal \naspect ratios (outside [0.10, 10.0]), or blade areas < 1% of the canvas \nwere filtered out. Together with a final QA step that excluded failed \nsegmentations and undersized masks, these procedures homogenized \nthe visual domain, enforced consistent orientation and background, \nand concentrated learning on diagnostically salient blade regions and \ntheir pamor textures. After this stage, the dataset was partitioned into \ntraining, validation, and testing sets using a stratified artifact-level split \nto prevent leakage, as detailed in Section 2.7."
    },
