    "depth": 0,
    "payload": {
      "content": "Augmentation began with pre-masking: binary blade masks were \nderived via near-white thresholding and were refined morphologically. \nThe geometric transformations included horizontal flips (𝑝= 0.5), small \nshift-scale-rotate operations (𝑝≈0.7, within ±6% shift/scale and ±5◦ ro-\ntation), and light perspective distortions (𝑝≈0.2). Photometric variants \napplied exclusively to blade pixels comprised brightness/contrast ad-\njustments (±20%), Gaussian blur (𝑘= 3), and Gaussian noise (variance \n10–50). Gaussian noise was selected as a conservative perturbation to \nemulate sensor-level variability. Other noise models (e.g., impulse or \nmultiplicative noise) were not pursued to avoid introducing unrealis-\ntic artifacts that could distort fine-grained blade textures. After each \nperturbation, the background was reset to a pure white background \nto prevent color leakage. Random scaling and coarse dropout were \ndeliberately excluded to maintain morphological fidelity."
    },
    "control_plane": {},
    "parent_node_id": null,
    "segment_index": 0,
    "segment_count": 1
  },
  {
