      "semantic_origin": "pdf_text"
    },
    "depth": 0,
    "payload": {
      "content": "precision and applied gradient clipping of 1.0. Models were optimized \nwith Adam under an exponential learning-rate decay, initialized at \n5×10−5 and decayed by 4% every 105 steps. Focal loss (𝛼= 0.25, 𝛾= 2.0) \nwith class weights proportional to the label frequencies was employed \nto address the class imbalance. Training ran for up to 100 epochs with \na batch size of 8, early stopping (patience 8), and ReduceLROnPlateau \n(factor 0.5, patience 4) while monitoring validation macro-F1. The \nbest model was checkpointed using the validation macro-F1. Random \nseeds were fixed across Python, NumPy, and the framework to ensure \nreproducibility. All experiments were repeated with three stratified \nresamplings of the train/validation split while keeping the held-out test \nset fixed, and results were reported on that fixed test set. Experiments \nwere conducted on Ubuntu 22.04.3 LTS (kernel 5.4.0–155) with 2×\nAMD EPYC 7742 CPUs (256 threads) and 1.0 TiB RAM. Training used \na single NVIDIA A100-SXM GPU (40 GB class; single-GPU allocation) \nwith driver 525.147.05 and CUDA 12.2 (nvcc 12.2.140). The imple-\nmentation used Python 3.10.12, TensorFlow 2.20.0 (tf-keras 2.20.1) for \nKerisRDNet, and PyTorch 2.0.1+cu117 for PyTorch-based baselines."
